| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-4)-(-6)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-12+12 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,0\\,|=0\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289213 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "288e49b0-f706-54de-86b7-a17248fe2408" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Parallelogram Spanned by Two Non-Parallel Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "556b4699-a3ea-5c69-88e0-00ec44a76a53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "556b4699-a3ea-5c69-88e0-00ec44a76a53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289215} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7167cb4-32e2-5cbc-a1bf-ff0a4c445670" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d3f06126-dd7a-58be-a1a3-c69ca4cf1a54" :question/math-academy-id "q-275539" :question/problem "Determine the area $A$ of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $\\text{v}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$\\,\\,A=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)-4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,-9\\,|=9\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289216 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "288e49b0-f706-54de-86b7-a17248fe2408" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Parallelogram Spanned by Two Non-Parallel Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff42ca44-dc1d-5e13-99a8-a52e9d30db21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289218} {:answer/id #uuid "6b3e234d-d2a8-5f59-8922-1eb77dd08dd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff42ca44-dc1d-5e13-99a8-a52e9d30db21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289218} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d19b4ca-11a1-569c-bf9c-65953d1bce47" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289217}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f76f30e6-ef9b-537f-bdbc-c545f6421b50" :question/math-academy-id "q-320413" :question/problem "Determine the area $A$ of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=⟨-4,-1⟩$ and $\\text{v}=⟨6,2⟩.$\n\n$\\,\\,A=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-4)\\cdot 2-6\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-8-(-6) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,-2\\,|=2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289220 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0272b8d6-8400-5a6d-b51d-fc6ca84bd166" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Parallelogram Spanned by Two Parallel Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5669635-9956-5e62-b8d3-ebc7c9ac5b32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289222}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5669635-9956-5e62-b8d3-ebc7c9ac5b32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289222} :answer-field/id #uuid "82129578-1092-5512-bc14-e44ab2f9fbe3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289221}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e3d7e857-f860-5925-9b71-d1c2560557c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-320558" :question/problem "Given that the area spanned between the vectors $\\text{u}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{7} \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $\\text{v}=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]$ equals zero, what is the value of $a?$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{7} & a \\\\ 5 & -10\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{7} & a \\\\ 5 & -10\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-\\sqrt{7})(-10)-a\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =10\\sqrt{7}-5a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, setting the expression for the determinant equal to $0$ and solving for $a,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10\\sqrt{7}-5a & =0 \\\\ 5a & =10\\sqrt{7} \\\\ a & =2\\sqrt{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289223 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0272b8d6-8400-5a6d-b51d-fc6ca84bd166" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Parallelogram Spanned by Two Parallel Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4099e5a5-1fa1-5823-989b-c8a7d95013ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289225} {:answer/id #uuid "69064473-d083-5ea4-8f2e-c7dc99465d2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289226} {:answer/id #uuid "e38bfd63-c2d3-5c3c-80a1-f031c69a84a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289227} {:answer/id #uuid "655c203c-44c2-5b17-bf1e-84f2228b36de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289228} {:answer/id #uuid "b52c58ab-c73c-56f7-bb21-ff4f2b4f460f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b52c58ab-c73c-56f7-bb21-ff4f2b4f460f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289229} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ff4e1ea-4485-5426-8afa-ceaa9528b770" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289224}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9954dfd3-7837-5aea-b973-57052f57e541" :question/math-academy-id "q-69946" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $\\text{v}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 4 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 4 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})-\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =1-1 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,0\\,|=0\n$$"}]}
